  "limitations": [
    "The six archived targets retain their original embedded producer configuration; diagnostic source equality does not requalify that configuration.",
    "Hydration and a forced full starting collection age each target graph before encoding, unlike native generation.",
    "Both modes force six terminal full collections; this is diagnostic cleanup and not ordinary writer policy.",
    "Two pairs on one six-target bundle do not establish corpus-wide performance or concurrency behavior.",
    "Callback and phase timing instrumentation adds overhead; OS caches and host contention are uncontrolled.",
    "Original manifest bytes are reused, so sample-payload recomputation and writer publication are not exercised.",
    "The cold profile used a different target bundle and post-generation GC state; its GC time is not directly interchangeable.",
    "A production pause needs bounded exact-native input eligibility, exception/restoration guards, and fresh native qualification."
  ],
